James Rising received an email from Tariq Chowdhury, a prospective PhD student for Fall 2026, expressing interest in joining his research group in Environmental Economics. Tariq highlighted shared research interests in climate impacts and economic modeling, referencing James's papers. James drafted a professional response, appreciating Tariq's interest but clarifying that he could not accept new students this year due to existing commitments. He encouraged Tariq to continue pursuing relevant research opportunities and offered to provide advice if Tariq wished to schedule a Zoom chat. James also permitted Tariq to mention his name in the application statement.
